  "about": "The fonts Windows 10 and 11 come with, by family name (the names a page asks for them by, the older ones a weight or width once had its own name under among them), and those Windows adds with a language (its supplemental fonts). Pages in Noor find these and no other font of the computer (see main/fonts.js). A family followed by style words only ('Segoe UI Semibold', 'Bahnschrift Light Condensed') counts as the family; a name that starts with one of the prefixes (families only Microsoft makes, whose older names Windows cuts to 31 letters: 'Segoe UI Variable Display Semib') counts too.",
